WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.636
-President Trump
traveled to Texas today

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.371
to make the case
for his border wall

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.039
as the government shutdown
dragged on.

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:09.375
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:13.646
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.948
This is now the second-longest
shutdown in history,

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.217
and the effects are very real
for millions of people,

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.420
from federal workers
about to miss paychecks

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.422
to potential cuts to housing
subsidies and food stamps.

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.558
Even our National Parks
are not immune.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.995
And now park visitors are
resorting to desperate measures.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:32.732
-16,000 of our
19,000 park employees

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.800
are no longer on their jobs.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.068
Along with all the others,

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:37.836
they've been deemed
nonessential.

00:00:37.836 --> 00:00:40.106
That means
roads are left unplowed,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.241
garbage is left uncollected,

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.844
bathrooms no longer work
or are being maintained.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.780
Trash is piling up,
there are health hazards,

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.216
and park visitors,
in some places,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.685
are taking care of business,
shall we say,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.754
along pathways or in the woods.

00:00:55.754 --> 00:00:57.289
-Great.
Now when someone says,

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:58.691
"Does a bear [bleep]
in the woods?"

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.793
you can say,
"Yeah, and so does Kevin."

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:03.129
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.965
The reality is that Trump
is subjecting millions of people

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.667
to unnecessary
pain and suffering

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.270
to get his wall and hoping
Democrats will blink first.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.572
Reporters asked him
if he could empathize

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.174
with people who, right now,
are literally having to choose

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.411
between food and medicine,
and he insisted that he could.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.747
-Mr. President, can you relate
to the pain of federal workers

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.215
who can't pay their bills?

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.651
-I can relate.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.854
And I'm sure that the people
that are on the receiving end

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:32.158
will make adjustments.
They always do.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.126
And they'll make adjustments.

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:36.629
People understand
exactly what's going on.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:41.433
But many of those people that
won't be receiving a paycheck,

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:45.905
many of those people
agree 100% with what I'm doing.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.007
-I don't know.
It's hard to imagine

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.709
someone sitting
at their kitchen table,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.978
choosing between food
and insulin, saying,

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.780
"I'm just glad
Trump's getting his wall.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.849
Now off to take a dump
in the park."

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.451
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.654
And also, no.
No, you cannot relate.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.289
You got a million dollars
from your dad,

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.291
you lived in a golden tower
for most of your life,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.126
and you've never
even been to a supermarket,

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.628
which we know,
because you once told a crowd

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:12.264
you need I.D. to buy groceries.

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:14.634
-You know, if you go out
and you want to buy groceries,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:18.771
you need a picture on a card.
You need I.D.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.073
-No, you don't.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.641
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.710
If you need an I.D.
to buy your groceries,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.913
you're an alcoholic.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.181
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.282
And --

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:34.019
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:35.822
And if you're a worker
going without pay,

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.458
it probably stings all the more
knowing Trump has no idea

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.926
what's actually happening
at the border.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.827
All he has are his delusions,

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.796
and those delusions are getting
weirder and weirder.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.732
Here he is yesterday describing
how he thinks migrants

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.534
get across the southern border.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:51.637
-The fact is that
if we don't have barriers,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.506
walls, call them what you want,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.942
but if we don't have
very strong barriers,

00:02:55.942 --> 00:03:00.446
where people can not any longer
drive right across --

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.214
They have unbelievable vehicles.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:03.349
They make a lot of money.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.851
They have the best vehicles
you can buy.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:08.121
They have stronger, bigger,
and faster vehicles

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.323
than our police have
and than ICE has

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.524
and than border patrol has.

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:14.560
-What are you talking about?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.997
They have unbelievable vehicles
that are faster than our police?

00:03:18.997 --> 00:03:21.700
Did you try to watch the news
and accidentally watch

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:22.935
the "Transformers" movie
instead?

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.370
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.806
"These immigrants, they have
unbelievable vehicles, folks.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.976
They can fly.
They can talk.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.778
They're friends
with Shia LaBeouf."

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.879
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:36.649
This is actually
a new obsession for Trump.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.184
For the last week or so,
he's been telling

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.019
very bizarre stories
about how migrants

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.355
are supposedly driving across
the Southern border.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:45.057
Here he is last week trying
to explain the route they take

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:46.392
to cross into the U.S.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.095
See if you can follow
any of this.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:52.899
-They get off the road, and
they drive out into the desert,

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.767
and they come on,
they make a left turn.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.535
Usually it's a left,
not a right.

00:03:56.535 --> 00:04:00.640
They make a right turn before
they get to the port of entry.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:06.278
They go as far as the wall is,
or as far as the barricade is,

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.781
and then they make a left.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.551
Welcome to the United States.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.519
-He sounds like Google Maps

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.988
after you drop
your iPhone in the toilet.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.322
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:21.093
"Hey, Siri, can you give me
directions to 30 Rock?"

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.963
-Get off the road.
Drive out into the desert.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.064
Make a left turn.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.567
Usually it's a left turn,
not a right.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.035
Make a right turn.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:31.603
Go as far as the wall,
then make a left.

00:04:31.603 --> 00:04:33.473
-Yeah, never mind.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:36.608
And that's not the only delusion
Trump has had about the wall.

00:04:36.608 --> 00:04:38.310
In that same
press conference last week,

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.413
he claimed
that previous presidents

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.315
had privately confessed to him

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.051
that they wished
they had built the wall.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:48.721
-This should've been done
by all of the presidents

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.790
that preceded me,
and they all know it.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.027
Some of them have told me
that we should've done it.

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.661
-Now that's an obvious lie,

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.396
and every living president
has denied it.

00:04:57.396 --> 00:04:58.864
But here's
what's so weird to me.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:01.433
Why didn't he just pick
a president who was dead?

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:04.771
It would've been so much easier
to get away with.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.071
"You know, right before he died,

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:09.074
Ronald Reagan told me
he wished he'd built a wall.

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.910
Now, you can't ask him
because he's dead,

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.411
but he totally said it.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:15.414
It was at a secret meeting
in a National Park

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:16.882
where we both took dumps."

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.918
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:22.721
It's impossible.

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:25.124
Fully impossible
to negotiate with someone

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.793
who doesn't operate on the same
plane of reality that you do,

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:31.130
which is why his trip to the
border today made no difference.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.199
On his way there,
he stopped by reporters

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:36.602
to once again argue that only
a wall would stop immigration,

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:39.772
adding that technology alone
would not work.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.308
-We need border security,
and have to have it.

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:45.377
And the only way you're
gonna have border security --

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:46.945
there's only one way.

00:05:46.945 --> 00:05:49.115
You can have all
the technology in the world.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.284
I'm a professional
in technology.

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.152
[ Laughter ]
-No, you're not, no.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.420
You don't know how to operate --

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.189
You don't even know
how to operate an umbrella.

00:05:57.189 --> 00:06:00.893
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:04.796
So, I mean...

00:06:04.796 --> 00:06:06.131
Look at how he's dressed.

00:06:06.131 --> 00:06:08.334
He looks like the only
technology he's familiar with

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.468
is a stair lift.

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:10.536
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.737
He shouldn't
be in the White House.

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:13.406
He should be at the
self-checkout aisle

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.474
in the grocery store,
yelling at the computer,

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:17.710
"Oatmeal! Oatmeal!"

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.777
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.777 --> 00:06:20.012
"I have I.D.!"

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:23.115
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:23.115 --> 00:06:25.318
And when Trump finally --

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:27.152
finally got
to Texas this afternoon,

00:06:27.152 --> 00:06:28.321
he held a roundtable

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:30.423
where he made a new argument
for the wall.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:36.228
Trump said, "Walls can't be bad
because cars have wheels."

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:38.063
-They say a wall is medieval.

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:39.632
Well, so is a wheel.

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:42.768
A wheel is older than a wall.

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:45.404
And I look
at every single car out there,

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:49.409
even the really expensive ones
that the Secret Service uses,

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:52.111
and believe me,
they are expensive.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.345
I said,
"Do they all have wheels?"

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.681
"Yes."
"Oh, I thought it was medieval."

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:56.916
The wheel
is older than the wall.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.484
You know that?

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.986
And there are some things
that work.

00:07:00.986 --> 00:07:04.457
You know what?
A wheel works and a wall works.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:07.526
-I'm sorry -- you had to look
at all the cars...

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:08.994
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:11.364
...to confirm they had wheels?

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.464
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.464 --> 00:07:13.633
Man, I take it back.

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:16.469
You are a real...
-Professional in technology.

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:18.404
-But, seriously,
what is wrong with your brain?

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.839
Did someone replace
your Diet Coke with Nyquil?

00:07:20.839 --> 00:07:22.441
I mean, honestly,

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:24.743
how long until he just starts
reciting nursery rhymes?

00:07:24.743 --> 00:07:28.080
"The buses,
they all have wheels, folks.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.715
And the wheels on these buses,
they go round and round."

00:07:30.715 --> 00:07:31.817
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:34.252
"Round and round.
Round and -- All!

00:07:34.252 --> 00:07:36.289
All through the town.

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:39.358
All through --
That's why we need a wall."

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.226
Trump is frustrated because
he's not winning the argument,

00:07:41.226 --> 00:07:42.295
and even he knows it.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:44.363
He spent three years
making the wall

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:47.466
the signature promise of his
campaign and his presidency

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:48.600
and it got nowhere.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:50.169
A majority of Americans
are against it.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.471
Democrats are now
in charge of the House.

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:55.674
And as we saw in November,
when voters go to the polls...

00:07:55.674 --> 00:07:56.742
-They make a left turn.

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:59.011
Usually it's a left,
not a right.

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.513
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:04.517
[ Cheers and applause ]

